[19:33:00] I redrew the burrito as a Solo48 model. It passes `validate_icon()` (valid, no warnings) and the build gate (`build_gate.py`: pass, no errors or warnings). I checked it at 48 px on a white background only; I didn't render a dark-theme version.

**Subject and keyshape:** an upright wrapped burrito with three filling lobes at the top, one diagonal fold and a curved flap. I used `VRECT_M`, the keyshape the metrics suggested. The walls sit on x=10 and x=38, the top of the middle lobe on y=4 and a round bottom (radius 14) on y=44, so all four edges of the box are hit exactly. It is symmetric left to right except for the fold and flap, which run diagonally.

**Metric issues, all fixed:**
| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| keyshape-short-axis (width only 65% filled) | Rebuilt at full width, without stretching the trace |
| Hole inside the filling lobes, 4.56 wide | Now 8.8 wide (limit 6) |
| Hole in the flap triangle, 3.58 wide | Now 6.7: the fold runs lower and the flap bows upward like the tortilla edge in the image |
| Spacing between parts: 7.05 and 6.22 (limit 8) | The fold and flap now meet the outline only at shared endpoints; the validator reports no spacing problems |
| Trace stroke 2.62 | Redrawn at stroke 4; all hole sizes above were measured at stroke 4 |

**Differences from the image:**
- In the image, the fold curls into the right wall halfway down. Here it runs straight to where the wall meets the round bottom, because the halfway landing makes the flap triangle too small for the 6-unit hole minimum.
- I compared three other versions: a curved fold, a fold with a bend where the flap meets it, and no flap. I dropped the curved and bent folds because they failed the 6-unit hole minimum, and dropped the no-flap version because it no longer read as wrapped.

Lucide has no burrito icon, so the shapes follow the generated image.

Files are in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260929-1919-burrito/`:
